.TH QWDOCTOR 1 "November 2026" "Local-LLM-Unsensored" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
qwdoctor \- diagnostic health check, Tor connectivity, and OPSEC verification tool
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qwdoctor
[\fB\-\-json\fR]
.PP
.B qw check
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B qwdoctor
(or
.BR "qw check" )
is a system diagnostic and OPSEC verification tool that validates the operational health of all Local-LLM-Unsensored services and security boundaries.
.PP
It verifies:
.IP \(bu 2
Tor SOCKS5h daemon connectivity on \fI127.0.0.1:9050\fR.
.IP \(bu 2
Remote DNS and exit IP masking via \fIcheck.torproject.org\fR to guarantee zero clearnet leaks.
.IP \(bu 2
Local \fBllama\-server\fR daemon responsiveness on port 8080.
.IP \(bu 2
GGUF model file availability and storage sizes.
.IP \(bu 2
CLL Web Gateway binding status on port 41625.
.IP \(bu 2
Active \fB.qwignore\fR and \fI~/.config/qw/ignore\fR rule integrity.
.IP \(bu 2
System Python runtime dependencies (\fIfastapi\fR, \fIuvicorn\fR, \fIrequests\fR, \fIbs4\fR).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
Output diagnostic results as a machine-readable JSON array.
.TP
.B \-h\fR, \fB\-\-help
Display command synopsis and exit.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR qwsearch (1),
.BR qwfile (1),
.BR qwsec (1),
.BR qwserver (1)
